{"AssignmentSource.dataclass uses timezone.now() as a default value which is evaluated at import time, so all instances get the same timestamp. Should use default_factory to evaluate per-instance.": 0.9590603113174438, "AssignmentSource.to_dict returns a datetime which will be put into Celery kwargs and JSON-serialized \u2014 datetime is not JSON-serializable by default, so enqueueing tasks will likely fail.": 0.8467414379119873, "Tests don't surface the JSON serialization problem because they don't assert task queue serialization. Should add a test that mimics serialization to detect the datetime issue.": 0.29598113894462585, "After changing to string serialization, tests that assert to_dict contains queued (as datetime) should be updated to expect a string": 0.2746841311454773}